# Client-app installers are BINARIES built from droplet-windows /
# droplet-android — they are never committed here (they'd bloat every
# clone, and this is not the repo that builds them).
#
# NOTHING STAGES THEM FOR YOU. There is no image-build step, no setup.sh
# path and no OTA payload that puts an installer in this directory; an
# operator runs scripts/app-downloads/stage.sh on the box. If you are
# reading this because /downloads is empty, that is why — see README.md,
# and `bash scripts/app-downloads/audit.sh` will tell you what this
# release is supposed to carry.
#
# Tracked here: only the hand-authored side of the contract, the docs,
# and EXPECTED — the per-platform declaration the auditor reconciles
# against what is actually staged.
*
!.gitignore
!README.md
!platforms.example.json
!EXPECTED
